           <button type="button" class="btn ghost small" id="transcribeTake" data-tip="SheetSage2 writes this take's own sound down as a score (the server reads the take itself; nothing is uploaded), into the form for a cover: with chords, or the melody only, as chosen under Cover a recording. Good for a reading made in Direct mode, which has no score.">Transcribe this take</button>
           <button type="button" class="btn ghost small" id="trimToText" data-tip="For readings and songs that go on past their text: Whisper finds where the text ends, and the same take is rendered again from its own music codes cut there (+1.5 s). The same performance, without the returns and babble after the last line; only the sound stage runs.">Trim to the text</button>
+          <button type="button" class="btn ghost small" id="endAt" data-tip="End the take at a moment: its last 2 s fade out, and nothing after it is kept. For a song that runs on past its proper end (in Full, the score's leftover bars after the last words). The moment is where the player stands when this take plays; otherwise you are asked. From the take's kept latents in seconds (the very sound), else its music codes rendered again. A new take; this one stays.">End at…</button>
